Spec: Ride outline

Purpose:
  The small stored geometry of one ride: its points simplified, encoded as a polyline and boxed.

Owns:
  ./ride_outline.dart
  /test/domain/ride_outline_test.dart

References:
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md
  /lib/features/history_map/history_map.sdd

Must:
  @RideOutline.simplify keeps the first and last point and drops every point that lies within `5` m of the
    line between its kept neighbours (Douglas-Peucker); the result never has more points than the input.
  An outline has at most `500` points: when `5` m leaves more, the tolerance doubles until it fits, so
    the stored text and the map data stay small on long rides.
  Fewer than two input points give an empty outline; two or more points that are all identical give two points.
  The encoded polyline uses the standard format with `5` decimal places; @RideOutline.decode of an encoded
    outline returns every point within `1` m of the original.
  @RideOutline.bounds is the box around all points as south, west, north and east.
  Distances use the shared @DistanceCalculator seam.
  @segmentDistanceM is the shared distance from a point to a segment; @OutlineHit and @AreaFilter reuse it.

Must not:
  Read trackpoints, the database or the clock.

Scenario: straight line with a dense middle
  Given points that lie on a straight line
  When they are simplified
  Then only the first and last point remain

Scenario: a corner larger than the tolerance
  Given points that turn by `30` m at one point
  When they are simplified
  Then that corner stays

Example:
  no points: empty outline
  one point: empty outline
  encode then decode: each point within `1` m
